phi-adapter-onkyo (0.0~git202609081014.9d0be55-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Connectivity is the TCP connection and nothing more: a receiver in standby
    accepts the socket and hangs up without answering, and stays connected,
    because a receiver you can reach is one you can switch on. Only a
    connection that cannot be made reads as disconnected.
  * The socket is half-closed and drained before it is let go. close() with
    unread data pending makes the kernel send a reset, which discards whatever
    of ours is not yet acknowledged - and the power write is the one command
    with nothing behind it to notice.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 10:14:29 +0200

